  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠BAC.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠BAC$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠CAD).$\n\nTherefore, the correct equation to determine $x$ is the following:\n\n$$\nx={70}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
